+# SPN-161 — Revoked socket closure across navigation
+
+## 📏 Scope and persona decision
+
+**2026-11-14, accepted registration; implementation and acceptance pending.**
+The agent delivery manager applies the owner's continuous backlog workflow and
+[standing four-persona authority](../todo/process.md#decisions). The reviewed
+failure handoff identifies a distinct session-revocation observation investigation
+exposed by SPN-128 validation. Register it on actual main before implementation;
+retain SPN-128's full L product outcome and add this actual verification prerequisite.
+It is not a new product dependency or a way to turn a failing gate into acceptance.
+
+The complete estimate is **M, pre-launch**: finite real-browser investigation,
+demonstrated narrow fixture correction if warranted, safe first-attempt evidence
+custody, focused positive/negative controls, integration and actual existing
+development/production two-login acceptance. Count native/authority/runtime
+investigation and independent exact-head review, not merely a helper edit. A
+confirmed product closure/authorization defect requires a new scope checkpoint
+before broader transport implementation; no unsupported product diagnosis is made.
+
+Options considered: an unchanged full-test retry cannot establish the missing
+first witness; accepting navigation/401 alone weakens the contract; opportunistic
+SPN-128 changes hide an independently owned security journey; a general observer
+framework is unjustified. The selected finite experiment preserves the original
+contract and permits only a demonstrated correction. Non-reproduction is retained
+and ends that sample, without speculative repairs or an automatic completion claim.
+
+**All four personas:** Operator (M) gains bounded truthful security evidence without
+document access. Owner (M) retains real revocation and saved-work protection.
+Collaborator (M) retains the other login's socket, queued edit and durable native
+content. Link guest is explicitly unaffected: existing capability denial/privacy
+remain unchanged, so no impact score or new authority is invented. The tradeoff
+is a separate M investigation and verification delay while its actual prerequisite
+is unresolved; neither historical causal certainty nor a relaxed gate is promised.
+
+## 🧾 Original failure and source provenance
+
+The original source is [d22baa6997e27c123ef351a8f5321089cc9e345b](https://github.com/mxbaylee/spinel/commit/d22baa6997e27c123ef351a8f5321089cc9e345b),
+base `8e9dccbd90f04ad79bd12cba3695e5c4ff04e02d`, tested merge
+`9b48767d1effc0aeb55f6020d8676427d74f7d9f`. [CI 43658210882 attempt 1,
+development 1/2 job 132641633704](https://github.com/mxbaylee/spinel/actions/runs/43658210882/job/132641633704)
+failed the flaky-test gate: 76 expected passes, four skips and one flaky case.
+The two-login case failed retry zero in **11,480 ms** at
+[`e2e/collaboration.spec.ts:462`](https://github.com/mxbaylee/spinel/blob/d22baa6997e27c123ef351a8f5321089cc9e345b/e2e/collaboration.spec.ts#L462):
+the unchanged **5,000 ms** poll did not observe every selected protocol socket
+closed. Retry one passed in **18,432 ms**; it does not replace the first failure.
+
+The first receipt records one target opened at 5,161 ms, edit-held and
+revocation-written at 6,383 ms, then main-frame navigation at 6,438 ms (+55 ms).
+It has no socket-closed/page-close event, one open/zero closed targets, six received
+frames, and observerLost/overflow/reopened all false. Later denial, queued-write,
+saved-reload and broadcast assertions did not run. Retry one's receipt records
+an observed close at 10,347 ms before navigation at 10,395 ms and the full contract.
+Both cleanup arrays remain retained. Only retry one has a trace ZIP; retry zero
+has two screenshots, error context and an inline content-free receipt. A trace
+for the first attempt must not be invented.
+
+The independent failure-audit report at
+`/tmp/spn128-terminal-d22baa69/audit-output/development-first-failure.json`
+was copied into the handoff as `independent-development-first-failure.json`:
+10,352 bytes, SHA-256
+`9b2e4bba33fb7bdc8dfe32363a396c36b131656eb40c030dd0e6f7e1a69daf29`.
+This is a derived audit, not the original Playwright reporter. The original
+artifact ZIP **14139456753** has SHA-256
+`2dfe9b8331b971d4e0ca92ded19d53918ea845a569b8829fcd310ee8fa5c335d`;
+its `playwright-report/development-1-of-2.json` member is 1,483,603 bytes,
+SHA-256 `edd0beae9188fff2171eb0d6dcd1455669bcf2f7cdf5d659b08d0a7d15acf29d`.
+That original reporter contains the inline observation receipts and actual
+attachment references from which the audit records the two attempts.
+The original artifact, derived audit and source-provenance handoff are retained
+locally; the later immutable failure archive is **pending**, not an existing
+link or acceptance claim. CI artifact retention is supplementary. Preserve the
+original observations separately from derived analysis and implementation evidence.
+
+All **16 direct/shared inputs** were independently byte-rechecked between main
+8e9dccbd and d22: `e2e/collaboration.spec.ts`, `e2e/session-revocation.ts`,
+`scripts/ci/session-revocation.test.ts`, `e2e/sync-network.ts`,
+`e2e/native-sheet-value.ts`, `playwright.config.ts`, `scripts/e2e.ts`,
+`scripts/e2e-server.ts`, `src/server/sync/transport.ts`, `src/server/auth/store.ts`,
+`src/server/collaboration/identity.ts`, `web/spinelSync.ts`,
+`lib/sync-client/index.ts`, `lib/sync-server/index.ts`, `package.json` and
+`package-lock.json`. Their blob/byte/hash binding is retained with the registration
+evidence. The observer/spec owner landed with SPN-149 at
+`a3dfc6f3373babecf979d5b851bbbf46c6dbb3b9`; keep its canonical history intact.
+SPN-128's supervised recovery fixture work does not own this security journey.
+Unchanged inputs establish provenance and ownership, not exclusion of every timing
+contribution or proof of the original connection's physical state.
+
+The helper already uses a direct CDP session rather than Playwright's per-document
+WebSocket map. Existing synthetic controls explicitly deliver a close event after
+navigation: they prove consumption, not real Chromium delivery. Production source
+revalidates access before sends/on its existing tick and requests close code 1008 for
+denied connections; that source behavior is not an observed close in this failed
+attempt. Do not claim a physical leak, successful original closure, or a pinned
+browser guarantee from current upstream source. Pinned Playwright **1.64.1** and
+Chromium **156.0.8078.4** (revision 1248) are retained runtime identities; no dependency
+was patched or installed for the diagnosis.
+
+## 🔬 Finite experiment before a repair
+
+After this registration lands and a separate implementation is scoped/reviewed,
+obtain the shared normal-pressure workload slot. Predeclare one small Chromium
+invocation using pinned Node 26.13.0/browser, the existing Playwright fixture and
+`observeSessionRevocation`, a task-owned loopback HTTP/ws server, one worker,
+no retries and **three fresh contexts/sockets**. No app build, install or cache
+mutation is part of this probe. Use a private cache, existing serial 2 GiB/eight-
+minute watchdog and **30-second outer probe bound**. Stop on the first setup,
+harness or resource error; this is a new controlled experiment, not a rerun of
+the failed hosted test.
+
+1. **Close-first control:** establish a real 101 socket and freeze its identity;
+   request server close code 1008, observe that exact server ws and underlying TCP
+   socket close, then navigate. Record direct CDP and page events. Require the
+   observer to recognize actual closure within the unchanged 5,000 ms deadline.
+2. **Navigation-first ordering:** establish a fresh connection and allow a real
+   new-document navigation with the same direct CDP observer. After that boundary,
+   request server close only if the connection still exists; otherwise record
+   that the browser physically closed it earlier. Use actual event barriers, no
+   sleep or navigation blocker. Record server ws/TCP and both browser streams;
+   a no-op close call cannot be represented as a new physical event. Compare the
+   actual ordering without asserting that the intended schedule occurred.
+3. **Live-socket negative:** establish a fresh real connection and deliberately
+   withhold close while returning an actual synthetic 401 HTTP response. The
+   observer must stay false/reject `assertRevoked(401)`; only then perform owned
+   cleanup. Navigation, denial, method invocation or cleanup closure never proves
+   the required protocol-close witness.
+
+If actual physical close is observed but direct CDP misses it, that demonstrates
+a present observation boundary, not the original attempt's physical outcome.
+Choose the smallest proven navigation-independent passive witness tied to that
+exact established connection. If CDP delivers the event but accounting fails,
+repair only demonstrated accounting. If physical closure/authority fails, stop
+for the product-scope checkpoint. Do not build a generic observation framework
+before this finite experiment establishes a need.
+
+## 🧪 Verification and diagnostic upkeep
+
+Extend the existing helper/control owners. Require negatives for absent/wrong/
+stale close, a live socket plus 401, closed socket plus 200, reopened connections,
+observer loss/overflow, late broadcasts and cleanup-only closure. Preserve the
+**5,000 ms closure** and **60-second journey** budgets, configured retries as
+separate failed attempts, fail-on-flaky behavior and all exact queued-write,
+server content, native reload, other-login continuity and authority assertions.
+
+After a demonstrated correction, the existing development and production owners
+each execute one retry-zero two-login case in the first reviewed candidate's
+hosted validation. This does not authorize narrowing unrelated selected work.
+Current source/shared routing must include helper, auth, transport, navigation,
+network/native fixtures, runtime and package/lock inputs; selected missing,
+failed, skipped or cancelled work must fail required aggregates. Synthetic
+controls and the small probe do not replace actual app/native acceptance.
+
+Keep a bounded snapshot before observer/context cleanup and retain cleanup
+separately without replacing the first error. Use one trace owner and actual
+uploaded filenames for retry-zero trace/receipt custody; body-only attachment
+assumptions are insufficient. Receipts include only ordinal identities, relative
+monotonic timestamps, kinds/counts and status/code, never URLs, request IDs,
+cookies/tickets, frame payloads or authored content. Bind exact helper/probe,
+source/base/tested/plan, runtime/browser/package/lock and original outputs.
+
+This registration changes no runtime or production emitter. Fixture-only
+observation work must document its inspected production no-impact decision;
+any actual observed transport/operation boundary change must update the
+[emitter inventory](../diagnostics.md#emitter-maintenance-inventory), content-free
+schema and meaningful observer-isolation regression evidence. Observation cannot
+affect the operation or become authority. No additional metrics are required by
+this documentation registration.
+
+The [focused registration record](grooming-revoked-socket-closure-2026-11-14.md)
+records allocation, dependency and check boundaries. No experiment, repair,
+native acceptance or completion is claimed by registration.
