+# 🔌 SPN-161 Verify revoked socket closure across navigation
+
+## Story
+
+As the [Owner](../product/personas.md#owner), I want revoking one login to prove that its actual connection closed even while it leaves the document, so that another login's queued work stays safe and later broadcasts cannot reach the revoked login.
+
+## Scenarios
+
+### Revocation remains provable when navigation wins
+
+Given two established logins and a queued native edit in the other login,
+When one login is revoked while its page navigates,
+Then the actual frozen connection identities have a physical-close witness and the revoked login receives 401,
+And the other login retains its socket, queued edit and exact saved/reloaded native value, with no later frame reaching the revoked connection.
+
+### Missing closure or authority never passes
+
+Given an absent, wrong or stale close, a live socket plus 401, a closed socket plus 200, an unauthorized reopen, observer loss/overflow or a later broadcast,
+When the revocation assertion runs,
+Then it rejects the incomplete evidence; navigation, a close-method call and cleanup-only closure cannot satisfy it,
+And the first failure and bounded receipt are retained before owned cleanup, whose result is recorded separately.
+
+## Rules
+
+- Follow [sustainable testing](../testing.md). Preserve the [complete M investigation, original incident and four-persona decision](../implementation/SPN-161.md#-scope-and-persona-decision), agent judgment under standing delegation, 2026-11-14. Link guest is explicitly unaffected; no impact score or capability change is invented.
+- The [original failure](../implementation/SPN-161.md#-original-failure-and-source-provenance) proves a missing observed close, not a physical leak or successful closure. Preserve SPN-149's prior history and both d22 attempts; retry success does not replace retry-zero acceptance. Unchanged inputs establish provenance, not historical causality.
+- Run the [declared three-case experiment](../implementation/SPN-161.md#-finite-experiment-before-a-repair) once before choosing a correction. Fix only a demonstrated observation/accounting boundary; if actual server closure or authority fails, stop and reassess the full scope before product changes. Non-reproduction ends the declared sample without speculative repair or repeat-until-green execution.
+- Retain the original 5,000 ms closure deadline, 60-second journey budget, fail-on-flaky gate, exact connection identity, all native/authority/content assertions and existing configured retries as separate attempts. No sleeps, navigation blocker, deadline increase, retry-based success or generic observation framework.
+- Receipts are passive, bounded and content-free: ordinal connection identities, relative monotonic timing, event kinds/counts and status/code only. Never retain URLs, request IDs, cookies/tickets, frame payloads or authored content. Inspect [diagnostic upkeep](../diagnostics.md#emitter-maintenance-inventory); explain unchanged production emitters for fixture-only work, or update inventory/schema/regression evidence when an actual observed production boundary changes.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- SPN-128's preserved-original recovery product work, a changed revocation policy, a provider/new browser matrix, dependency upgrades and a general monitoring framework. Registration completes neither ticket.
+
+## Verify
+
+- Contract/negative owners: extend `scripts/ci/session-revocation.test.ts` and `e2e/session-revocation.ts` for absent/wrong/stale closure, live-plus-401, closed-plus-200, reopen, observer loss/overflow, late broadcast and cleanup-only closure; synthetic event injection alone does not prove browser delivery.
+- Real boundary owner: the predeclared close-first, navigation-first and live-socket-negative Chromium experiment, fresh real 101 connections, actual server ws/TCP and direct-CDP/page events, one worker/no retries/30-second outer bound, existing normal-pressure 2 GiB/eight-minute serial watchdog. Preserve failures before stopping observers/contexts; close only owned resources.
+- Integration owner: the existing two-login case in `e2e/collaboration.spec.ts`, once at retry zero in each existing development and production owner on the reviewed candidate. Preserve 401, real closure, other-login continuity, queued-write delivery, exact server/native reload and no-late-broadcast assertions; configured retries remain separate failures.
+- Source/shared selection: observer/controls, collaboration/navigation/sync-network/native helpers, server/auth/transport/identity, sync-client entries, runtime/Playwright config and manifest/lock inputs. Preserve automatic ownership and selected-missing/failed/skipped/cancelled rejection; do not narrow CI to make the gate pass.
+- Evidence: exact source/base/tested/plan/runtime/browser identities, declared experiment and every actual ordering/result, first-attempt trace/receipt under one trace owner with real uploaded filenames, untouched original failure/retry limits, bounded cleanup and current-head native acceptance. [Full evidence contract](../implementation/SPN-161.md#-verification-and-diagnostic-upkeep).
